    {
      "event": "delta",
      "delayMs": 70,
      "data": {
        "text": "**Mitosis** and **meiosis** both copy a cell's DNA and divide its nucleus. "
      }
    },
    {
      "event": "delta",
      "delayMs": 70,
      "data": {
        "text": "Mitosis involves one division and usually produces two genetically identical cells "
      }
    },
    {
      "event": "delta",
      "delayMs": 70,
      "data": {
        "text": "with the same number of chromosomes as the original. It helps organisms grow and repair tissues.\n\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "event": "delta",
      "delayMs": 70,
      "data": {
        "text": "**Meiosis** involves two divisions and usually produces four genetically different cells, "
      }
    },
    {
      "event": "delta",
      "delayMs": 70,
      "data": {
        "text": "each with half the original number of chromosomes. In animals it makes sex cells such as sperm and eggs. "
      }
    },
    {
      "event": "delta",
      "delayMs": 70,
      "data": {
        "text": "During meiosis, matching chromosomes can swap pieces of DNA, which creates genetic variation.\n\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "event": "delta",
      "delayMs": 70,
      "data": {
        "text": "The short version: mitosis makes copies, meiosis makes variety."
      }
    },
